{{!
    @template plagiarism_essayguard/student_signal_contributions

    The four signal families that make up a score, each as a bar.

    A summary of the numbered signal table that follows it, not a replacement: the table
    remains the evidence. This answers "what is driving this score?" at a glance.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * contributions - Array of bars, each with:
        * key - Family key: observed, behavioural, style or comparative.
        * label - Family name.
        * sublabel - What the family measures.
        * points - Points contributed.
        * max - The most this family can contribute.
        * pct - points as a percentage of max, 0-100.
        * fired - Whether this family contributed anything.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "contributions": [
            {"key": "observed", "label": "Observed",
                "sublabel": "Clipboard use and bulk insertion",
                "points": 34, "max": 40, "pct": 85, "fired": true},
            {"key": "comparative", "label": "Comparative",
                "sublabel": "Departure from this learner's earlier work",
                "points": 12, "max": 15, "pct": 80, "fired": true}
        ]
    }
}}
<h4 class="essayguard-contrib-heading">{{#str}}contrib_heading, plagiarism_essayguard{{/str}}</h4>
<div class="essayguard-contrib">
    {{#contributions}}
    <div class="essayguard-contrib-row">
        <div class="essayguard-contrib-text">
            <span class="essayguard-contrib-label">{{label}}</span>
            <span class="essayguard-contrib-sub">{{sublabel}}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="essayguard-contrib-track" role="img"
            aria-label="{{label}}: {{points}} of {{max}}">
            <div class="essayguard-contrib-fill essayguard-contrib-fill-{{key}}"
                style="width: {{pct}}%"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="essayguard-contrib-value essayguard-contrib-value-{{key}}">
            {{#fired}}+{{points}}{{/fired}}{{^fired}}0{{/fired}}
        </div>
    </div>
    {{/contributions}}
</div>
<p class="essayguard-contrib-note">{{#str}}contrib_reviewnote, plagiarism_essayguard{{/str}}</p>
